class.description:
Provides read-only introspection over GDScript types and the helpers used to build dynamic proxies. It is exposed as the [code]reflection[/code] member of the [code]godot[/code] namespace, so it is called as [code]godot.reflection.method(...)[/code]; you never construct it yourself.
A [i]dynamic proxy[/i] is a synthetic object that statically satisfies a trait or abstract type and routes every call in that type's contract through a handler [Callable]. The proxied type must be a trait or abstract type whose native base is [RefCounted] or a [RefCounted]-derived type such as [Resource]; the proxy host is then a real instance of that native base, so [code]is[/code] checks and native methods against it hold. Non-reference-counted bases ([Object], [Node], ...) are not supported. The same primitive serves mocking (the handler records calls and returns stubbed values) and Spring-style interception/AOP (the handler logs or times a call and then "proceeds" to a real target).
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# Mocking: a handler records calls and returns stubbed values.
var stub: Dictionary = {"find": "stubbed"}
var repo := godot.reflection.create_proxy_dynamic(Repository, func(method: StringName, args: Array):
    return stub.get(method, null)
) as Repository

# Interception/AOP: a handler logs a call and proceeds to a real target.
var real := UserService.new()
var logged := godot.reflection.create_proxy_dynamic(UserService, func(method: StringName, args: Array):
    print("calling ", method)
    return real.callv(method, args)
) as UserService
[/gdscript]
[/codeblocks]
Reflection introspection accepts either a script type (a [Script]) or an instance, whose script is used. The descriptors it returns use the same [Dictionary] shapes as [method Object.get_method_list] and [method Object.get_property_list].
